# [[.Name]] — a scantor script ([[.Language]])

This folder is a scantor script: it evaluates the results and files of your scans on the platform. The
definition lives in `main.py`; `scantor-script.yaml` is the manifest; `models.py` holds the result model
of the task whose scans the script reads.

Commands:
- `scantor scripts push .` — upload the folder
- `scantor scripts run . --scan <scanId> --limit 100 --follow` — try it on 100 analyses
- `scantor scripts run . --scan <scanId> --follow` — run it on every analysis
- `scantor scripts runs logs <runId> --follow` — follow a run's log

Rules: keep `name` in scantor-script.yaml unchanged; paste the task's result model into `models.py`;
functions passed to `ctx.map` with `processes > 1` must be module-level and return picklable values;
use `ctx.checkpoint` and `ctx.resume_state` so a restarted run can resume; secrets come from
`ctx.secrets`, never from the config.

Python: the config derives from `scantor.Config` and gives every field a default; the result is any
pydantic model; list extra packages in `requirements.txt` (never pydantic).

